Subject: [PATCH] bin: let a distribution package satisfy the default agent

omarchy-default-agent reaches mise for any agent without an explicit
agent_installer, and already declines to shadow an install mise did not make --
see user_install and its comment. A distribution package is the same case, and
on an architecture the agent's publisher does not build for it is the only case
that can arise: mise's backends resolve release assets by platform, so
`omarchy default agent crush` on powerpc64le fails with

    no asset found: crush_0.98.1_Linux_powerpc64.tar.gz

even though /usr/bin/crush exists and is current, built from the source tarball
Charm does publish alongside those binaries.

distro_install() is checked after user_install, so a deliberate ~/.local/bin
install still wins, and before mise, so the packaged build is preferred over a
copy mise would have to fetch. It looks at /usr/bin and /usr/local/bin by path
rather than through `command -v`, so a stale mise wrapper in ~/.local/bin
cannot hide the package behind it.

Not ppc64le-specific in form: on x86_64 the loop simply finds nothing for agents
Omarchy does not package, and the behaviour is unchanged.

Rebased onto 4.5.0, where presence is `mise where "$agent_tool"` and install
goes through omarchy-mise-default-tools; both now consult distro_install first.

--- a/bin/omarchy-default-agent
+++ b/bin/omarchy-default-agent
@@ -102,7 +102,23 @@
   user_install() {
     [[ -x $HOME/.local/bin/$agent ]] && ! mise_wrapper "$HOME/.local/bin/$agent"
   }
-  agent_present() { user_install || mise where "$agent_tool" &>/dev/null; }
+  # An agent shipped as a distribution package is an install mise did not make
+  # and must not shadow, for the reason given above. On architectures the
+  # agent's publisher does not build for, it is also the only install that can
+  # exist: mise's backends resolve release assets by platform, so selecting
+  # Crush on powerpc64le fails with
+  #   no asset found: crush_0.98.1_Linux_powerpc64.tar.gz
+  # while /usr/bin/crush is present and current, built from the source tarball
+  # upstream does publish. Checked by path rather than through `command -v` so
+  # that a stale wrapper left in ~/.local/bin cannot hide it.
+  distro_install() {
+    local p
+    for p in /usr/bin/"$agent" /usr/local/bin/"$agent"; do
+      [[ -x $p ]] && pacman -Qoq "$p" &>/dev/null && return 0
+    done
+    return 1
+  }
+  agent_present() { user_install || distro_install || mise where "$agent_tool" &>/dev/null; }
   # Omarchy declares the default agents as mise tools, so installing one is
   # enough and leaves the user's config alone. A user who removed the
   # preinstalls, like one without Omarchy's declarations, selects it instead.
@@ -112,7 +128,7 @@
     [[ $1 == npm:* || $(mise tool "${1%%\[*}" --backend 2>/dev/null) == npm:* ]]
   }
   agent_install() {
-    user_install && return
+    { user_install || distro_install; } && return
     if omarchy-mise-default-tools declares "$agent_tool"; then
       if npm_backed "$agent_tool"; then
         mise install node "$agent_tool"
